.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-network-config [interface]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
interface   Device name of the network interface
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-network-config
command is an interactive user interface for configuring a
network interface.  It prompts the user for IP address, netmask,
router, etc., and then configured and enables the network interface.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-network-config re0
auto-network-config wlan0
.ad
.fi

